limit and without the exclusion in the first paragraph of this Section, to pay, for the whole period of a use outside the licenses granted in this EULA, the price of the license or upgrade that covers that use, determined as the USE BEYOND THE LICENSE paragraph of Section 1.1 states for a purchase made on the date of OPTIMAJET’s notice of that use, and, unless Developer End User committed to buy within the periods of the USE BEYOND THE LICENSE paragraph, interest on that price at the rate that the PAYMENT paragraph of Section 1.1 states from the date on which that use started. Developer End User also remains liable, without the liability limit and without the exclusion in the first paragraph of this Section, to pay the price of each license, renewal, option, and other purchase that it bought or committed in writing to buy under this EULA, a quote, or an order, as far as that price is due, whether or not it disputes the payment. This Section 13 limits the money that a party pays to the other. It does not limit injunctive or other non-monetary relief, termination under Section 15, or a party’s obligations to stop a use, to destroy copies and confirm their destruction, and to keep information confidential. A breach of a party’s rights in its software, source code, or confidential information may cause it harm for which damages are not an adequate remedy.

## 14. INDEMNIFICATION

IP CLAIMS. An “IP Claim” is a claim by a third party that the SOFTWARE DEVELOPMENT PRODUCT(S), as provided by OPTIMAJET and used in accordance with this EULA, infringes that third party’s patent, copyright, or trademark or misappropriates its trade secret, where the claim is made against Developer End User, against its Affiliates that use the SOFTWARE DEVELOPMENT PRODUCT(S) under its license, or against the officers, directors, or employees of any of them. Developer End User will notify OPTIMAJET in writing of an IP Claim as soon as reasonably practicable after it becomes aware of it and will give OPTIMAJET the information about it that OPTIMAJET reasonably requests, other than information protected by legal privilege or that a court order or a duty of confidentiality forbids it to give. OPTIMAJET may take part in the defense of an IP Claim with its own counsel at its own cost, and Developer End User will not admit on OPTIMAJET’s behalf that the SOFTWARE DEVELOPMENT PRODUCT(S) infringes. OPTIMAJET has no obligation to defend anyone against an IP Claim or to pay damages, costs, or settlements on it, and its only obligations for an IP Claim are those in the REMEDIES FOR AN IP CLAIM paragraph, unless OPTIMAJET and Developer End User agree otherwise in a written agreement signed under Section 16; Developer End User may ask OPTIMAJET for such an agreement, for example together with an option that raises the liability limit under Section 13.

REMEDIES FOR AN IP CLAIM. If an IP Claim is made or, in OPTIMAJET’s reasonable opinion, is likely, OPTIMAJET may, at its option and expense, either obtain for Developer End User the right to continue using the affected part, or modify or replace that part so that it no longer infringes and keeps materially the same functionality. If neither is feasible with commercially reasonable efforts, OPTIMAJET may end the license concerned by notice and, if it does, will refund, for a perpetual license, its net price, reduced by one fifth for each full year since OPTIMAJET first issued its license key, together with the net price paid in advance for the unused part of a prepaid update period of that license and, for an annual subscription, only the net price paid in advance for its unused part. That termination takes effect ninety (90) days after OPTIMAJET’s notice, or earlier where a court order or a settlement that binds Developer End User requires it; until then Developer End User may continue the Production Use of the versions that it uses on the date of the notice, and of the security updates that Section 15 describes, only to migrate away from the SOFTWARE DEVELOPMENT PRODUCT(S), as Section 15 describes that use, and OPTIMAJET will pay the refund when the license ends. For a Form Engine license included in a license of Workflow Engine NEO, that refund is of the net price of that license of Workflow Engine NEO and is due only if Developer End User also ends that license. If a court finally holds that the SOFTWARE DEVELOPMENT PRODUCT(S) infringes, or an order of a court or a public authority, including a preliminary injunction or a judgment enforceable pending appeal, bars Developer End User from using it because of an IP Claim, in proceedings of which Developer End User notified OPTIMAJET under the IP CLAIMS paragraph, and OPTIMAJET has not done one of these within sixty (60) days after Developer End User’s written notice of that holding or order, Developer End User may end the license concerned and receive that refund.

EXCLUSIONS. OPTIMAJET has no obligation under the REMEDIES FOR AN IP CLAIM paragraph for an IP Claim to the extent that it: (a) does not identify the SOFTWARE DEVELOPMENT PRODUCT(S) as the basis of the claim; (b) arises from a combination of the SOFTWARE DEVELOPMENT PRODUCT(S) with software, hardware, data, or processes that OPTIMAJET did not provide, where the claim would not have arisen without that combination; (c) arises from Modifications or another change that OPTIMAJET did not make, where the claim would not have arisen without them, or from use after OPTIMAJET gave notice under the REMEDIES FOR AN IP CLAIM paragraph that it ends the license concerned; (d) concerns use under the Form Engine Non-commercial License or under the EVALUATION paragraph of Section 1.1, any other use for which no price was paid (the use of a Form Engine license included in a license of Workflow Engine NEO is not such a use), or a third-party component under Section 7; or (e) arises from the parts of a Licensed Product other than the SOFTWARE DEVELOPMENT PRODUCT(S) as provided by OPTIMAJET, from the data, content, or materials of Developer End User or its End Customers, or from a breach of this EULA by Developer End User. This Section states OPTIMAJET’s entire liability, and Developer End User’s only remedies, for claims that the SOFTWARE DEVELOPMENT PRODUCT(S) infringes the rights of others, unless a written agreement signed under Section 16 provides otherwise.

INDEMNITY BY DEVELOPER END USER. Developer End User will defend OPTIMAJET and its officers, directors, employees, agents, and representatives against any claim made by a third party to the extent that it arises from (i) a use of the SOFTWARE DEVELOPMENT PRODUCT(S) by or for Developer End User in breach of this EULA, or (ii) a Licensed Product, or an application built under a license for which no price was paid, including claims by its End Customers, but, for the copy of another person’s product that Developer End User licenses under the INTEGRATORS AND RESELLERS paragraph, only to the extent that the claim arises from Developer End User’s own use, data, configuration, or changes of that copy, and will pay the damages, costs, and reasonable attorneys’ fees finally awarded or agreed in a settlement that Developer End User approves, except to the extent that the claim arises from the SOFTWARE DEVELOPMENT PRODUCT(S) as provided by OPTIMAJET and used in accordance with this EULA, provided that:

(a) OPTIMAJET notifies Developer End User in writing of the claim as soon as reasonably practicable after it becomes aware of it, and a delay relieves Developer End User of its obligations only to the extent that the delay prejudices the defense;

(b) OPTIMAJET does not admit any liability for the claim or agree to any settlement or compromise of it without Developer End User’s prior written consent, which Developer End User will not unreasonably withhold or delay;

(c) Developer End User has the exclusive conduct of the defense and settlement of the claim, but it will not agree to a settlement that requires OPTIMAJET to admit fault, to pay an amount that Developer End User does not pay, or to take or stop any action without OPTIMAJET’s prior written consent, and OPTIMAJET may take part in the defense with its own counsel at its own cost; and

(d) OPTIMAJET gives Developer End User the assistance that Developer End User may reasonably require in connection with the claim, at Developer End User’s expense.

A contractor that holds a license for a client under the CONTRACTOR-HELD LICENSES paragraph of Section 1.1 gives the indemnity under the INDEMNITY BY DEVELOPER END USER paragraph only for its own acts, and not for claims about the use of the Licensed Product after the reissue of that license.

## 15. TERMINATION

Without limiting any other rights or remedies, OPTIMAJET may terminate a license granted under this EULA by written notice if Developer End User materially breaches this EULA in relation to that license and does not cure the breach within thirty (30) days after receiving a written notice that describes the breach. Developer End User’s other licenses are not affected. For an intentional breach, OPTIMAJET may terminate immediately by written notice: (i) this EULA and every license under it, other than the licenses that Developer End User holds for clients under the CONTRACTOR-HELD LICENSES paragraph of Section 1.1, which point (c) of that paragraph governs, if Developer End User uses the SOFTWARE DEVELOPMENT PRODUCT(S), the Source Code, or Modified Software in breach of Section 1.2; and (ii) the licenses concerned, if Developer End User breaches point (a) or (c) of Section 1.4 or discloses or distributes the Source Code in breach of Section 1.3. A breach is intentional only where Developer End User knew that its conduct breached this EULA, or continues that conduct after OPTIMAJET’s written notice that describes the breach; for this purpose, Developer End User knows what its license contact, its legal contact, or a manager responsible for the Licensed Product or for the product in which that conduct takes place knows; conduct that Developer End User reasonably and in good faith believed to be permitted is not an intentional breach before that notice, and continued use during a good-faith dispute under the USE BEYOND THE LICENSE paragraph of Section 1.1 is not an intentional breach while that dispute is pending. If a termination under this paragraph is found not to meet its conditions, it takes effect as a notice of breach under the first sentence of this Section. A disclosure of the Source Code is not a ground for immediate termination if, within five (5) business days after Developer End User becomes aware of the disclosure, it removes the disclosed Source Code from public access or, where it was disclosed to particular persons without the authorization of its license contact, its legal contact, or a manager responsible for the Licensed Product or for the product in connection with which it was disclosed, obtains their written confirmation that they have deleted it and have not used it, and notifies OPTIMAJET, or if a person to whom Developer End User gave access made the disclosure without Developer End User’s authorization and Developer End User takes reasonable steps to stop the disclosure once it becomes aware of it.

Developer End User may terminate a license by written notice if OPTIMAJET commits any of the following breaches and does not cure it within thirty (30) days after receiving a written notice that describes it: (a) it does not issue a license key that the Licensed Product needs within the Licensed Use, the Domains, and the features that the license permits (Section 1.4), other than a key that the PAYMENT or CONTRACTOR-HELD LICENSES paragraph of Section 1.1 or Section 11 allows OPTIMAJET to withhold; (b) it does not make available, during a period that Developer End User has paid for, the updates and, where the license includes source code access, the Source Code; (c) it receives data from the SOFTWARE DEVELOPMENT PRODUCT(S) contrary to the LICENSE KEYS AND DATA paragraph of Section 1.1; (d) it names Developer End User as a customer although it and Developer End User have signed a non-disclosure agreement at Developer End User’s request, or more than thirty (30) days after a request to stop under Section 9, or shows Developer End User’s content without its consent, contrary to Section 9; or (e) it treats as a Competing Product a product that it confirmed in writing under Section 1.2 is not one. Developer End User may also terminate a license by written notice if a supervisory authority with jurisdiction over Developer End User requires it in writing, or if a law, a regulation, or an order of a public authority that applies to Developer End User, including sanctions laws, prohibits it from continuing to use the SOFTWARE DEVELOPMENT PRODUCT(S) or to deal with OPTIMAJET or its successor. In each of these cases, OPTIMAJET will refund the net price paid in advance for the unused part of an annual subscription or a prepaid update period of that license. Developer End User may also terminate a license, other than a license that it holds for a client under the CONTRACTOR-HELD LICENSES paragraph of Section 1.1, at any time by written notice to OPTIMAJET, without a refund and without release from its obligation to pay the price of any term of an annual subscription that it committed in writing to buy; where it so terminates an annual subscription, or a license paid in installments before it is paid in full, it and the copies of its End Customers then have only the rights that they have when such a license ends without renewal or full payment, and not the twelve (12) months that this Section gives after a termination. Where it so terminates a license during an intentional breach for which the first paragraph of this Section allows OPTIMAJET to terminate that license immediately, or during a failure to pay that the PAYMENT paragraph of Section 1.1 makes a material breach, this Section applies as if OPTIMAJET had terminated that license for that breach or that failure to pay. No other breach by OPTIMAJET gives Developer End User a right to terminate, except under Sections 12 and 14 and except a right to terminate for good cause that the law governing this EULA does not allow to be excluded, which gives the same refund. No refund of the price of a perpetual license is due except under Section 12 or 14.

On termination of a license, or of this EULA, Developer End User must stop using and distributing the SOFTWARE DEVELOPMENT PRODUCT(S), the Source Code, and Modified Software under the terminated licenses, and destroy the copies of them and of the related documentation that it holds under those licenses, except as the following paragraphs permit.

Copies of a Licensed Product that Developer End User delivered to End Customers or installed in their environments before termination, or before a license paid in installments ends without full payment, with license keys that OPTIMAJET issued for that Licensed Product, remain licensed to the End Customers that did not take part in a breach of this EULA and that comply with the terms that point (b) of the DISTRIBUTION AS PART OF A LICENSED PRODUCT paragraph of Section 6 requires. After a license paid in installments ends without full payment, they remain licensed for ninety (90) days, and OPTIMAJET will issue to such an End Customer, on request, a license key for its copy that remains valid for those ninety (90) days. After a termination or such an end, or if Developer End User becomes insolvent, such an End Customer may buy from OPTIMAJET, at the price in the price list, a license for the copy that it uses, of a type listed in Section 18 whose Licensed Use, Domains, and features cover its own use of that copy, and may have that copy maintained by its own contractors. Unless OPTIMAJET terminated immediately for an intentional breach under the first paragraph of this Section, and except after a termination with a refund under Section 12 or, beyond the period that Section 14 allows, under Section 14, Developer End User may, for twelve (12) months after termination, continue to maintain and support those copies for those End Customers, using the SOFTWARE DEVELOPMENT PRODUCT(S) and Modified Software only for that purpose.

Unless OPTIMAJET terminated the license for an intentional breach or for a failure to pay under the PAYMENT paragraph of Section 1.1, and except after a termination with a refund under Section 12 or, beyond the period that Section 14 allows, under Section 14, Developer End User may also, for twelve (12) months after termination, continue the Production Use of the versions that it used on the termination date, and of the security updates that mandatory law requires OPTIMAJET to provide free of charge, with the license keys that they need, within the Licensed Use and usage limits of the terminated license, including a hosted service for its existing End Customers where that Licensed Use includes one, only to migrate away from the SOFTWARE DEVELOPMENT PRODUCT(S) and without new development or new deployments, other than corrections of defects and security vulnerabilities in the Licensed Product, the restoration of the copies then in use after a failure, including in a replacement environment, and the tools that the migration needs, such as tools that export data or move running processes. Developer End User may keep one archival copy where a law or a litigation hold requires it, solely for that purpose and not for any production or development use. Within thirty (30) days after the periods that this Section permits end or, where none applies, after the termination, Developer End User will confirm in writing that it has destroyed the Source Code and Modified Software in source code form, except that archival copy. Where a license that includes source code access ends because it is not paid in full, or an annual subscription that includes it ends without renewal (where a public body, or the holder of a license to which the PUBLIC BODIES paragraph of Section 1.1 applies the periods of a public body, has committed in writing to a renewal under the RENEWAL PRICES paragraph of Section 1.1, when the period for that renewal ends without it), Developer End User will destroy the Source Code and Modified Software in source code form that it holds under that license and confirm it in the same way. Copies in backup or archive systems that are not accessible in the ordinary course of business may be kept until they are deleted in the ordinary course, and Developer End User may keep its Modifications in a form that does not contain, reproduce, or translate the Source Code; the CONFIDENTIALITY paragraph of Section 1.3 continues to apply to them.

The expiration, non-renewal, or termination of a paid license does not by itself end the separate free rights to Public Source Code under Section 1.3. Public Source Code and Modifications to it retained or shared solely under those separate rights need not be destroyed, and a confirmation of destruction under this Section identifies that exception. Those rights do not permit continued commercial Production Use, continued use of a refunded license, or development or deployment of a Licensed Product for which Section 1.1 requires renewal. Subject to the separate platform rights recognized in Section 1.3, if OPTIMAJET terminates the separate Public Source Code rights for a breach under this Section, Developer End User must stop exercising those rights and remove the copies it made publicly available to the extent it controls them; that termination does not cancel rights already granted directly by OPTIMAJET to recipients who comply with this EULA. Receiving another copy or accepting this EULA again does not reinstate rights terminated for breach without OPTIMAJET’s written agreement. The destruction and confidentiality obligations for non-public Source Code remain unchanged.

Developer End User may at any time, including after a license ends or is terminated, export its data and the data of its End Customers, including its and their form definitions and the data entered in forms from its own databases and files, and this EULA does not restrict that export; this paragraph gives no right to use the SOFTWARE DEVELOPMENT PRODUCT(S), the Source Code, or Modified Software beyond what the rest of this Section 15 permits.

The following survive termination: (a) Sections 1.2, 2, 8, 11, 12, 13, 14, and 16; (b) the DISTRIBUTION AS PART OF A LICENSED PRODUCT paragraph of Section 6, for the copies that End Customers keep; (c) the LICENSE KEYS AND DATA paragraph of Section 1.1; (d) the rules of Section 9 on OPTIMAJET naming Developer End User and showing its content and on the ownership of the SOFTWARE DEVELOPMENT PRODUCT(S); (e) the OWNERSHIP, CONTRIBUTIONS, CONFIDENTIALITY, and COMPLIANCE CONFIRMATION paragraphs of Section 1.3; (f) the rules of this Section 15 on refunds, on the export of data, and on the copies of End Customers; (g) for the maintenance, support, and migration that this Section 15 permits after termination, the LICENSE paragraph of Section 1.3 and Sections 1.4, 5, and 6; and (h) the PAYMENT and TAXES paragraphs of Section 1.1, for amounts due under this EULA.

## 16. MISCELLANEOUS

The legal terms of this EULA may be modified only by a written agreement signed by Developer End User and an authorized officer of OPTIMAJET, or by a new version of this EULA that applies under the NEW VERSIONS paragraph of this Section. A written agreement signed in that way that amends or supplements this EULA, such as an addendum for a Licensed Product, prevails over this EULA for the matters it covers. Otherwise, the following order of precedence applies, from highest to lowest: (1) the License Statement, as corrected under this paragraph to match an accepted quote or order, for the scope of a license (Developer End User, the license, the Licensed Use, the Licensed Product, the Domains, and the periods); (2) a quote, order, or agreement for a license that OPTIMAJET issues and Developer End User accepts in writing, including electronically, for its prices, terms of payment, discounts, and renewal prices; (3) the price list on the date of purchase, for prices, Domains, update periods, and features; and (4) this EULA. The RENEWAL PRICES paragraph of Section 1.1 prevails over (2) and (3) for a renewal of the same scope, and Section 17 prevails over (3) for what each usage type covers. Where a License Statement differs from a quote or order that OPTIMAJET issued and Developer End User accepted in writing, OPTIMAJET will correct it to match at no charge, and until then that quote or order governs; a quote or order of a reseller or a contractor does not bind OPTIMAJET. A manifest error in a License Statement or a quote, such as a license type, a Licensed Use, or a price that does not match the purchase that both parties intended, is corrected to match that purchase. OPTIMAJET’s Commercial Support Agreement for Form Engine, published at https://optimajet.com/products/formengine/csa/, in the version in force when the support plan was bought until that plan is renewed, governs support services and prevails over this EULA for them, whether or not it is signed, but it neither reduces nor extends the versions that a license covers under the UPDATES AND PERPETUAL USE paragraph of Section 1.1, and it does not reduce the support that Section 18 includes, and the GOVERNING LAW AND DISPUTES paragraph of this Section governs disputes about support services. Despite the Commercial Support Agreement for Form Engine, OPTIMAJET’s liability for support services does not exceed the net price of the support plan, or of the license that includes the support, under which they are provided, and OPTIMAJET’s total liability for one event, under this EULA and for support services together, does not exceed the higher of the liability limit and that amount. These limits are subject to the exceptions and refund rules in Section 13, and do not reduce a refund of the net price paid in advance for an unused support period that is due under the applicable support agreement. Terms in the purchase orders or similar documents of Developer End User, of a reseller, or of a contractor do not apply, except as the PUBLIC PROCUREMENT LAW paragraph provides. If any provision of this EULA is held void or unenforceable, it is replaced by the enforceable provision closest to its purpose, and the rest of this EULA remains valid and enforceable according to its terms. This replacement does not apply where the law governing that provision does not allow it. If any remedy provided is determined to have failed of its essential purpose, all limitations of liability and exclusions of damages set forth in Sections 12 and 13 remain in effect.

NOTICES. A written notice under this EULA may be given by email. OPTIMAJET will send notices to the license contact and to any legal contact named in the License Statement or, after a change, in Developer End User’s later notice to OPTIMAJET or, where neither names a contact, to the email address that Developer End User last gave OPTIMAJET, and it will also send notices of breach or termination to the purchaser named in the License Statement. Developer End User will send notices to OPTIMAJET at hello@optimajet.com. A notice sent by email takes effect on the next business day after it is sent, unless the sender receives a message that it was not delivered. If Developer End User has not told OPTIMAJET of a change of its license contact or legal contact, a notice sent to the contact on record takes effect as if it had been delivered; where OPTIMAJET receives a message that such a notice was not delivered, it will also send a copy to the email address from which Developer End User last wrote to OPTIMAJET, and that copy does not change when the notice takes effect. A notice to Developer End User takes effect even if its copy to the purchaser is not sent or not delivered. Developer End User may name a security contact, such as its Authorized Contractor, in the License Statement or by notice to OPTIMAJET, to receive the notices of Section 12 together with the license contact. OPTIMAJET processes the contact details of the persons named in a License Statement or in a notice as its privacy notice at https://workflowengine.io/agreements/policy/ describes. A notice that this EULA requires OPTIMAJET to give to all its licensees, such as a notice under Section 11 or the SUCCESSORS paragraph, is given by email to the license contacts on record of paid licenses and by publication on formengine.io.

