NEW VERSIONS. OPTIMAJET may publish new versions of this EULA. The separate free rights to Public Source Code are granted under the version of this EULA that OPTIMAJET includes with that code when it publishes it. A later change to a repository or website does not replace that version for a copy already received. An existing paid license may benefit from the new Public Source Code rights only together with their conditions; those rights do not extend its commercial scope, covered versions, or update period, or displace a signed agreement that prevails under this Section. A new version applies to a license already granted only to the extent that it gives Developer End User more rights, or if Developer End User accepts it in writing, including by accepting a quote that names it; OPTIMAJET will include in that quote, or link from it, a summary of the changes from the version that governed the license. A right that a new version grants subject to conditions, obligations, or limits applies to a license already granted only together with them, wherever this EULA states them. A renewal of updates, of the Source Code Window, or of an annual subscription, and a new purchase, are a new grant of the license under the version of this EULA that Developer End User accepts in writing for it, including by accepting a quote or an order that names it or by accepting that version when it buys online; a renewal for which Developer End User does not accept a new version continues under the version that governed the license. Otherwise the version in force when the license was granted continues to govern that license; installing a later version of the SOFTWARE DEVELOPMENT PRODUCT(S) within a paid update period does not change it. Use under a Form Engine Non-commercial License is governed by the version of this EULA in force on the release date of the version of the SOFTWARE DEVELOPMENT PRODUCT(S) that Developer End User uses, as the version history published with this EULA shows, or, for a version released before April 7, 2025, by Version 1.5 of this EULA. Where a signed agreement with OPTIMAJET names a version of this EULA, that version also governs Developer End User’s use under a Form Engine Non-commercial License.

