PUBLIC PROCUREMENT LAW. Where Developer End User is a public body, the following apply instead of the conflicting terms of this EULA, to the extent that the law, regulations, or binding procurement rules that govern its procurement require them: (a) the law that governs its procurement governs this EULA, disputes go to the courts of that jurisdiction or to its statutory claims process instead of arbitration under the GOVERNING LAW AND DISPUTES paragraph, and nothing in this EULA waives its immunity; (b) it gives the indemnity under the INDEMNITY BY DEVELOPER END USER paragraph of Section 14, answers for other persons under Sections 1.1, 1.3, and 13, and is liable beyond the liability limit of Section 13 only to the extent that its law permits; (c) it accepts this EULA only through a signed order, agreement, or contract that incorporates it or, for the Form Engine Non-commercial License, for evaluation, and for a build that it receives for acceptance under Section 6, through the written notice of acceptance that the first paragraph of this EULA describes, or, for a purchase in OPTIMAJET’s online store, through acceptance at checkout by a person authorized to make that purchase for it, and not by installation or use; (d) it may disclose the Source Code and other information as its public records law requires; for non-public information, it does so after claiming the exemptions for trade secrets and confidential commercial information that the law allows and giving OPTIMAJET notice that lets OPTIMAJET seek the protection of its confidential information; (e) if the funds for a later fiscal period of an annual subscription or of an installment plan are not appropriated, it may end that license or plan at the end of the period paid; the license then ends with that period and, under an installment plan, does not become perpetual; (f) it may transfer a license, together with the Licensed Product or the part of it that serves the transferred functions, by written notice to OPTIMAJET, to a public body that takes over those functions by law, and where a Licensed Product is divided between several bodies, each part needs its own license; (g) the terms of its order, agreement, or contract that the law, regulations, or binding procurement rules that govern its procurement require, such as termination for its convenience at the end of a period paid, limits on the termination or the transfer of a perpetual license, consent to an assignment by OPTIMAJET, and access to OPTIMAJET’s records of the purchase, prevail over this EULA, but no such term obliges OPTIMAJET to defend or indemnify anyone, raises the liability limit, adds a warranty, or gives a refund beyond the net price paid in advance for an unused period; and (h) where Regulation (EU) 2024/903 requires it to share a Licensed Product with another public body, it may share its own code and documentation; the SOFTWARE DEVELOPMENT PRODUCT(S) and the Source Code are third-party intellectual property that restricts sharing within Article 4(1) of that Regulation, and the receiving body needs its own license for use beyond the separate free rights to Public Source Code under Section 1.3.

GOVERNMENT END USERS. The SOFTWARE DEVELOPMENT PRODUCT(S) is commercial computer software, and its documentation is commercial computer software documentation. U.S. Government end users acquire them only with the rights set out in this EULA, as 48 C.F.R. 12.212 and 48 C.F.R. 227.7202 provide. A term of this EULA that federal law makes unenforceable against the U.S. Government does not apply to it. The SOFTWARE DEVELOPMENT PRODUCT(S) is a proprietary software package that OPTIMAJET sells to the general public at its catalog or market prices. A public body may grant a federal agency that funds a Licensed Product the rights that 2 C.F.R. 200.315 or 45 C.F.R. 95.617 require in its own code and its Modifications, marked as containing OPTIMAJET’s confidential information where they contain non-public parts of the Source Code, but no right in the Source Code or in the SOFTWARE DEVELOPMENT PRODUCT(S) beyond the rights independently granted under this EULA.

SUCCESSORS. This EULA binds OPTIMAJET and its successors and assigns. A merger, a change of control of OPTIMAJET, or a sale of the SOFTWARE DEVELOPMENT PRODUCT(S) to another owner does not end, shorten, or narrow any license already granted under this EULA, including perpetual licenses. OPTIMAJET will notify Developer End User of a change of control of OPTIMAJET within thirty (30) days after it. OPTIMAJET may assign this EULA only together with the SOFTWARE DEVELOPMENT PRODUCT(S), and only to a successor that agrees in writing to be bound by it, and will notify Developer End User of the assignment by email to the license contact within thirty (30) days after it.

